{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":482684,"name":"michael pulley","username":"michael_pulley","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/m/91b2a8/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-03T22:40:08.471Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482684-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482684-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482684-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482684-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFirst-time Grok Bot setup on Mac. The app never finishes connecting to Grok Bot cloud computer. Retry loops. No Bots were created.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExact screens, in order:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCan’t Reach Grok Bot’s Computer. Canned text about firewall, VPN, or proxy such as Zscaler. Retry.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAfter quit plus sign out/in: Can’t reach your computer. Your Bots are safe, they just can’t be loaded right now. Recover keeps files/logins and removes installed apps. Recover was NOT used.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eStill stuck: Reconnecting to your computer… / No saved Bots yet. Retry does nothing. Same on house Wi-Fi and on a phone hotspot.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is first-time setup. There is no existing Agent Computer that we can see.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482684-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482684-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSigned in via official onboarding only. Cursor account is michaelpulley at \u003ca href=\"http://proton.me\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eproton.me\u003c/a\u003e. Data sharing left OFF. Did not buy Cursor Pro.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eInstalled Grok Bot for macOS. First version 0.36.0; app later auto-updated to 0.39.0. Same failure.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFull quit (Cmd+Q), sign out, sign in again, wait a minute. Still can’t reach / reconnecting.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eConfirmed: no VPN, Mac firewall off, no HTTP proxy.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePhone hotspot (Verizon) — same error.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSet Wi-Fi DNS to Cloudflare 1.1.1.1 and Google 8.8.8.8, flushed cache, quit and reopened Grok Bot. Same error.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eHouse Wi-Fi again with those DNS servers still set. Still reconnecting. No saved Bots yet.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDid NOT click Recover computer or Reset.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNetwork checks (house Wi-Fi and hotspot):\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ethe us8 and us10 cursorvm test hosts resolve\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eHTTPS HEAD to the us8 cursorvm test host returns HTTP 404, Server awselb/2.0\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ethe bare cursorvm name has no A record on 8.8.8.8 and 1.1.1.1 (expected)\u003cbr\u003e\nSo this Mac can reach Cursor’s regional VM load balancer. The canned Zscaler/firewall text does not match this network.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482684-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482684-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter first sign-in, Grok Bot should finish creating or connecting the Agent Computer so I can create the first Bot. Retry should not loop forever on a machine that can already resolve and HTTPS-reach the us8 and us10 cursorvm hosts.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482684-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482684-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMacOS\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482684-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482684-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot:\u003cbr\u003e\nVersion: 0.39.0 (first install was 0.36.0; auto-updated)\u003cbr\u003e\nRelease Track: stable\u003cbr\u003e\nOS: darwin / macOS (Apple Silicon)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCursor account email: michaelpulley at \u003ca href=\"http://proton.me\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eproton.me\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482684-for-ai-issues-which-model-did-you-use-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482684-for-ai-issues-which-model-did-you-use-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFor AI issues: which model did you use?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok (Grok Bot). Not using Cursor IDE for this.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482684-for-ai-issues-add-request-id-with-privacy-disabled-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482684-for-ai-issues-add-request-id-with-privacy-disabled-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFor AI issues: add Request ID with privacy disabled\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003en/a — Grok Bot never connected, so there is no Request ID.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482684-additional-information-9\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482684-additional-information-9\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease check whether an Agent Computer exists for this account and rebuild it on your side if it is stuck in a partial first-setup state.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSame-day Cursor status incident covering Grok Bot and Cloud Agents was marked resolved at 17:07 UTC Sep 3 (incident id dj4cgfmwgm65). First attempt was after they marked it resolved. Status page now says All Systems Operational, but this account’s computer still never loads.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI can paste nslookup if needed. Please do not tell me to Recover/Reset first. Recover was offered, not used, because this is first setup and Recover does not create a missing computer.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-482684-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-10\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-482684-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-10\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-09-04T04:59:23.228Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":119,"reads":9,"readers_count":8,"score":596.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":170509,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-39-0-first-setup-reconnecting-to-your-computer-forever-mac","display_username":"michael pulley","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://proton.me","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Proton: Privacy by default","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":136043,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-39-0-first-setup-reconnecting-to-your-computer-forever-mac/170509/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":482821,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-04T04:55:33.841Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the detailed report. The diagnostics really helped. You’re right, it’s not your network. Your Mac can reach our servers fine, and the firewall/VPN/Zscaler text is misleading and not related to your case.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat’s happening: your account still doesn’t have an explicit Privacy Mode choice saved. During onboarding you only confirmed the data notice, but the actual choice didn’t get recorded. Grok Bot on your computer needs a saved privacy choice before it can connect, so connection attempts get rejected and the app stays on Reconnecting. Retry / Recover / Reset won’t fix this, so you were right not to touch them.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHow to unblock:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn your browser, go to \u003ca href=\"http://cursor.com/dashboard\"\u003ecursor.com/dashboard\u003c/a\u003e and sign in with your email.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen Settings and find the Privacy section.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePick Privacy Mode, keep data sharing off, and confirm.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFully quit Grok Bot with \u003ccode\u003eCmd+Q\u003c/code\u003e, then open it again.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf it still shows Reconnecting, click Retry once.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt should connect within a minute and let you create your first bot. If it still doesn’t work, send the attempt time with your timezone and we’ll dig in.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-09-04T04:55:33.841Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":6,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":31.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":170509,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-39-0-first-setup-reconnecting-to-your-computer-forever-mac","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://cursor.com/dashboard","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":20}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-39-0-first-setup-reconnecting-to-your-computer-forever-mac/170509/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":485728,"name":"Liam B","username":"Liam_B","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/l/ad7895/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-07T19:44:43.588Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI have the exact same issue and tried your above solution to no effect. I am using a Mac and I cannot get it to start it just keeps saying “reconnecting to your computer”. I asked LLM how to fix this and it told me to add 1.1.1.1 and 8.8.8.8 to DNS servers which now allows me to open the grok bot app but i am still stuck with “reconnecting to your computer…”. I have tried updating my privacy settings but this has not worked either.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-09-07T19:44:43.588Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":10.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":170509,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-39-0-first-setup-reconnecting-to-your-computer-forever-mac","display_username":"Liam B","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":136689,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-39-0-first-setup-reconnecting-to-your-computer-forever-mac/170509/7","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":489128,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-11T16:55:04.817Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey Liam. Quick note on DNS first: 1.1.1.1 or 8.8.8.8 don’t matter here, the issue isn’t network related. You can safely change those settings back, they won’t affect the connection.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo debug your specific case, I need a couple things:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePlease confirm that on \u003ca href=\"http://cursor.com/dashboard\"\u003ecursor.com/dashboard\u003c/a\u003e under Privacy you actually selected and saved Privacy Mode. This is different from just accepting the data notice during onboarding. After saving, fully quit Grok Bot with \u003ccode\u003eCmd+Q\u003c/code\u003e, then open it again.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSend the email for the account you’re using to log into Grok Bot.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eShare the time of your last connection attempt with timezone, and your Grok Bot version Stable and the build number.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith that info, we can check on our side what’s blocking the connection. Please don’t use Recover or Reset yet, they won’t help in this state.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":8,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-09-11T16:55:04.817Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":7,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":0.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":170509,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-0-39-0-first-setup-reconnecting-to-your-computer-forever-mac","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://cursor.com/dashboard","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"","reply_to_user":{"id":136689,"username":"Liam_B","name":"Liam B","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/l/ad7895/{size}.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-0-39-0-first-setup-reconnecting-to-your-computer-forever-mac/170509/8","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null}],"stream":[482684,482821,485728,489128]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,9],[3,5],[4,1]],"suggested_topics":[],"tags":[{"id":416,"name":"grok-bot","slug":"grok-bot"},{"id":408,"name":"networking","slug":"networking"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"fancy_title":"Grok Bot 0.39.0 first setup: Reconnecting to your computer forever (Mac)","id":170509,"title":"Grok Bot 0.39.0 first setup: Reconnecting to your computer forever (Mac)","posts_count":4,"created_at":"